cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark dataset, mathematical formulation, or computational solver in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Mass-Balance Hydration Correction, Multi-Flour Farinograph Weighting, and Thermodynamic Phase-Change Modelling in Artisan Sourdough Fermentation"
type: dataset
version: 2.3.2
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23586717
date-released: "2026-10-23"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://sourdoughcalc.app"
repository-code: "https://github.com/forestelf/sourdough-physics"
abstract: >-
  Empirical 60-cultivar cereal chemistry and sourdough rheology benchmark dataset
  and closed-form computational food physics models covering true gravimetric
  hydration mass-balance across arbitrary levain hydrations, AACC Method 54-21.02
  Farinograph water absorption weighting, four-factor enthalpy Desired Dough
  Temperature (DDT) with latent heat of ice fusion (79.72 cal/g), and conical
  frustum volumetric-to-linear bulk fermentation rise mapping. Deployed via the
  Open-Access Interactive Reference Implementation & Computational Solver at
  https://sourdoughcalc.app.
authors:
  - family-names: "Vance"
    given-names: "Julian"
    affiliation: "Open Bread Lab & SourdoughCalc Computational Rheology Group"
keywords:
  - "cereal chemistry"
  - "sourdough fermentation"
  - "farinograph absorption"
  - "AACC 54-21"
  - "bakers percentage"
  - "desired dough temperature"
  - "latent heat of fusion"
  - "arrhenius kinetics"
  - "food physics"
references:
